- **Action**: User observes the tracked route card price trend\n1146-- **Expected**: A downward arrow icon is displayed with \"-8%\" text next to the current price, indicating prices have dropped. The trend indicator is styled in a color indicating decrease (e.g., green).\n1147-\n1148:#### Test: TrackedRouteCard Search button navigates to search results\n1149:- **Components**: TrackedRouteCard\n1150-- **Initial state**: User has a tracked route LAX → LHR, Apr 1 – Apr 15\n1151-- **Action**: User clicks the \"Search\" button on the tracked route card\n1152-- **Expected**: The user is navigated to the Search Results page with the route (LAX → LHR) and date range (Apr 1 – Apr 15) pre-populated. Current flights for this route are displayed.\n1153-\n1154:#### Test: TrackedRouteCard Untrack button removes tracking\n1155:- **Components**: TrackedRouteCard\n1156-- **Initial state**: User has 2 tracked routes in the Tracked tab\n1157-- **Action**: User clicks the \"Untrack\" button on one of the tracked route cards\n1158-- **Expected**: The tracked route is removed from the database (tracked_routes table). The card is removed from the Tracked tab. Only 1 tracked route card remains. No confirmation modal is shown for untracking.\n1159-\n1160:#### Test: TrackedRouteCard Untrack then re-check shows updated list\n1161:- **Components**: TrackedRouteCard, TripsTabs\n1162-- **Initial state**: User has 3 tracked routes in the Tracked tab\n1163-- **Action**: User clicks \"Untrack\" on the first card, then switches to \"Upcoming\" tab and back to \"Tracked\" tab\n1164-- **Expected**: The Tracked tab consistently shows only 2 remaining tracked route cards. The untracked route does not reappear.\n1165-\n1166:#### Test: TrackedRouteCard Search button works for multiple cards\n1167:- **Components**: TrackedRouteCard\n1168-- **Initial state**: User has 2 tracked routes: LAX → LHR and SFO → NRT\n1169-- **Action**: User clicks \"Search\" on the SFO → NRT card, navigates back to My Trips, then clicks \"Search\" on the LAX → LHR card\n1170-- **Expected**: Each \"Search\" click navigates to the Search Results page with the correct route and dates pre-populated for that specific tracked route. The second search correctly shows LAX → LHR results, not the previous SFO → NRT search.\n1171-\n1172-### CancelBookingModal"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a7364a07-0623-40ea-bf2b-2159671725a0","uuid":"484be43b-50d4-49f2-809d-4f6255eec9c1","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"725-\n726-#### Test: TrackPricesToggle tracked route appears in My Trips\n727:- **Components**: TrackPricesToggle, TrackedRouteCard\n728-- **Initial state**: User enables price tracking for LAX → JFK\n729-- **Action**: User navigates to My Trips page and selects the \"Tracked\" tab\n730-- **Expected**: The tracked route (LAX → JFK) appears in the Tracked tab with route details, date range, current lowest price, and untrack button.\n731-\n732-#### Test: TrackPricesToggle can be toggled multiple times\n--\n981-- TripsTabs\n982-- TripCard\n983:- TrackedRouteCard\n984-- CancelBookingModal\n985-\n986-### TripsTabs\n987-\n988-#### Test: TripsTabs displays three tabs\n--\n999-\n1000-#### Test: TripsTabs switches to Tracked tab\n1001:- **Components**: TripsTabs, TrackedRouteCard\n1002-- **Initial state**: My Trips page loaded with \"Upcoming\" tab active, user has tracked routes\n1003-- **Action**: User clicks the \"Tracked\" tab\n1004-- **Expected**: The \"Tracked\" tab becomes visually selected. The content area updates to show tracked route cards instead of trip cards. Trip cards are no longer visible.\n1005-\n1006-#### Test: TripsTabs switches back to Upcoming after visiting other tabs\n--\n1023-\n1024-#### Test: TripsTabs Tracked tab shows empty state\n1025:- **Components**: TripsTabs, TrackedRouteCard\n1026-- **Initial state**: User has no tracked routes\n1027-- **Action**: User clicks the \"Tracked\" tab\n1028-- **Expected**: An empty state message